{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"attack","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDivisions","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDivisionsV","text":"MXLDivisions","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"attack"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Alters the starting time of the note from when it would otherwise occur, expressed in divisions. A note that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stops a tie should not have an attack attribute."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/attack"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV6attackAA12MXLDivisionsVSgvp","title":"attack","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"attack","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDivisionsV","text":"MXLDivisions","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"property"},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/attack"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLNote","abstract":[{"text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/attack":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Alters the starting time of the note from when it would otherwise occur, expressed in divisions. A note that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stops a tie should not have an attack attribute."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/attack","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"attack","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDivisions","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDivisionsV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"attack","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/attack"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDivisions":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLDivisions","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDivisions","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The divisions type is used to express values in terms of the musical divisions defined by the divisions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element. It is preferred that these be integer values both for MIDI interoperability and to avoid roundoff"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"errors."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDivisions"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDivisions"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldivisions"}}}